{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466904-worldbuilding-for-a-w-ta-5e-module","id":1466904,"title":"Worldbuilding for a W:tA 5E module","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-05T22:52:27-07:00","id":1466904,"title":"Worldbuilding for a W:tA 5E module","content":"After being on the sidelines ever since Forsaken came out, I gotta say I'm all in on 5th edition, 100%. Haven't made an account til now but here we are. I'm feeling so inspired by the news of changes I'm starting to world build for a module. I wanna hybridize Rite of Passage with Valkenburg Foundation and make a new kinda introductory chronicle thats tailored for people who've never played a World of Darkness game before. I feel like there's so much forgotten history in some of the original root modules when first edition came out that made for some really engaging storytelling. Like... What if you were a highschooler, and a guy named Sam in your dad's hunting clup hired you to hunt wolves with him. Lets say, the highschool mascots are the Red Talons, named after the wolves surrounding town that attack lumber workers.<br /> <br /> You could take it retro even, right back to the 80s. That's really hip right now, with the Stranger Things appeal to tabletop gaming. I can see ways this small town beyond just werewolves can introduce the character to mages, vampires, and even ratkin. And what more, what if the PCs start as mortals, OG ghoul stats, and the first change only really happens at the apex of the story? I guess in that way we're kinda flipping the two modules in order, doing valkenburg foundation first, and THEN rite of passage. The notion of the werewolves not being in the best shape sounds, frankly, like a total blast and I'm all in.<br /> <br /> Instead of a full familial sept you have a ragtag trio bone gnawer theurge, a ratkin runnel runner, and a glasswalker galliard conspiracy theorist that runs the community radio station and their collective level 1 purified junkyard meeting up with the gangrel at the local aloha lanes on the edge of town to plan raids on the local lumber companies. I feel like now couldn't be a better time to bring back Apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}